{"name":"Sunbathing Beauty","hex":"#7e4730","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sunbathing","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of lying outdoors exposed to the sun, usually wearing little or no clothing, especially in order to get a tan."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of sunbathe"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sunbathing"},{"term":"beauty","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The quality of being (especially visually) attractive, pleasing, fine or good-looking; comeliness.","Someone who is beautiful."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Thanks!","Cool!"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beauty"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sun tanning","blocks":[{"text":"Sun tanning or tanning is the process whereby skin color is darkened or tanned. It is most often a result of exposure to ultraviolet (UV) radiation from sunlight or from artificial sources, such as a tanning lamp found in indoor tanning beds. People who deliberately tan their skin by exposure to the sun engage in a passive recreational activity of sun bathing. Some people use chemical products that can produce a tanning effect without exposure to ultraviolet radiation, known as sunless tanning."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Tan_lines_on_human_female_chest.jpg/330px-Tan_lines_on_human_female_chest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sun_tanning","wikidata":"Q321458"},{"title":"Beauty","blocks":[{"text":"Beauty is commonly described as a feature of objects that makes them pleasurable to perceive. Such objects include landscapes, sunsets, humans and works of art. Beauty, art and taste are the main subjects of aesthetics, one of the fields of study within philosophy. As a positive aesthetic value, it is contrasted with ugliness as its negative counterpart."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Rozeta_Pary%C5%BC_notre-dame_chalger.jpg/330px-Rozeta_Pary%C5%BC_notre-dame_chalger.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beauty","wikidata":"Q7242"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Skin_tanning.JPG/500px-Skin_tanning.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Skin_tanning.JPG/1280px-Skin_tanning.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Skin_tanning.JPG/500px-Skin_tanning.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A sun tanned arm showing browner skin where it has been exposed","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASkin_tanning.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Photoaging.jpg/330px-Photoaging.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Photoaging.jpg/330px-Photoaging.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Photoaging of a woman","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APhotoaging.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Melanin_production_as_a_result_of_tanning.jpg/500px-Melanin_production_as_a_result_of_tanning.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Melanin_production_as_a_result_of_tanning.jpg/500px-Melanin_production_as_a_result_of_tanning.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cross-sectional view showing skin tone becoming darker due to the production of more melanin to overcome DNA damage caused by UV radiation","link":"ht